The search is `design/wiring/text-pass-work/search_replaced.py` (its 33 patterns are in the script; the files searched are the files I own, without cell.md). Run once in the middle (`search1.log`) and once on the final files (`search_final.log`): the last line of `search_final.log` reads `hits OPEN 23 HISTORY 62`. A hit is HISTORY when its line carries a marker word (before, history, superseded, replaced, old, was, earlier, stale, CLOSED, no longer, a version tag) and OPEN when it does not; the 23 OPEN lines are each read below. None is an unexplained use of a replaced value:
- architecture.md 206, 376 and main-board.md 61: my own text that names DBG_RX and TP22 to say they are dropped.
- mic-path.md 74, 126, 161 (two hits): my own text that names Gore, 6-layer and "at most 0.10 thick" to say they are replaced.
- mic-path.md 167: a quote of the architecture line the study asked to change (section 9 item 8, a list of changes "not made here"); the architecture line itself now says "older text, replaced by 17.19" (architecture.md line 422).
- architecture.md 330 and 360: section 16.2 and 16.4 (the A4-draft slim ring, "board 6 layers"); section 16 is the earlier draft that section 17 replaces (architecture line 411 "The thin ring ... (A5-draft)"); the current board is stated in 17.x lines 458 and the plan rows.
- band-liner.md 21, 27, 30, 31; body.md 23; cover-glass.md 44, 54: the pointer "open point 5" on these pages is right (band-liner point 5 is the tolerance of thickness and inner diameter; body point 5 is a tolerance tighter than ISO 2768-f; cover-glass point 5 is the glass outline). The wrong pointers of body.md (rows for the board, foam, adhesive, liner, flex, and line 113) are corrected (edit table).
- assembly.md 65 and draw.py 44: DAM1 "UV-cured dam": the dam material is not chosen (lead-decisions.md item 45 sets the sealant of the floor slots and the motor window, not the dam; open item S26 keeps it).
- light-path.md 15, 57, 60, 148: the pattern "X -12.7" matches the coordinates X -12.765 of the removed light guide; not the antenna place.
The 62 HISTORY hits are lines that carry the new value and name the old one as old (the style of the existing lines), or older sections of the design record; they are listed one by one in `search_final.log`.
